# nvfbc-relay policy replay fixture
# Get Medieval (KCD), 31 min of real streamed gameplay, b:vsync on the defaults (source rate not declared, 60 assumed; comb lock, 75 ms extra lag, flip timing and dejitter on) with capture through Windows.Graphics.Capture (-wgc) and the frames a mouse pointer move brings left out, 2026-10-12, build 407caaf; cut to the stretch the stream's video shows, 45.2 s to 1908.0 s
# units: microseconds. first value absolute, rest are deltas.
description Get Medieval (KCD), 31 min of real streamed gameplay, b:vsync on the defaults (source rate not declared, 60 assumed; comb lock, 75 ms extra lag, flip timing and dejitter on) with capture through Windows.Graphics.Capture (-wgc) and the frames a mouse pointer move brings left out, 2026-10-12, build 407caaf; cut to the stretch the stream's video shows, 45.2 s to 1908.0 s
# What the RELAY did on this capture. The replay model is only trustworthy
# for a configuration where it reproduces these; the test checks that.
field_worst_run 20
field_long_runs 0
field_synth_pct 0.5
field_pull_wraps 29
#
# WHAT IT COVERS: a whole stream of 31 minutes, cut to what its video shows, and the first
# captured through Windows.Graphics.Capture. The ring's frames came from WGC's pool, and the
# frames WGC delivers for a move of the mouse pointer alone were left out before the ring, 4338
# of them over the run, so the arrivals here are the game's pairs: 99.9% of the batches are
# pairs, 0.27 ms apart at the median. The policy is the one the tree ships. The game hitched 178
# times an hour and stalled for 100 ms or more 68 times an hour, with no periodic stretch. The
# stalls come in bursts. Eight times, from 334 s to 1498 s, a burst of three to five hitches
# with two stalls of 337 to 440 ms is followed 7 to 21 s later by two hitches with one stall of
# 190 to 280 ms. Two more bursts, 1025.7 s to 1045.2 s and 1082.3 s to 1087.2 s, hold 21 hitches
# and 9 stalls of up to 350 ms, and the last two stalls are at 1636 s and 1666 s. The one lock
# release is at 735.05 s, right after a pull wrap down at 734.75 s and one back up at 735.00 s.
# The worst blend run, 20 presents from 1087.15 s, starts as the second of those two bursts
# ends. Of the 67 moves on the replay, 2 land more than 2 ms from a real frame, at 1847.05 s and
# 1847.07 s, one inside the other's window.
#
# WINDOW. The video pairs with this log at log time = video time + 45.155 s, from the 2716 marked
# frames in its first 45 s, which sit within 0.45 ms of that offset (p90). The video runs 1881.5 s
# with no holes. Its first frame is gameplay; its last 16 s show the inventory and a document, so
# the cut ends at 1908.0 s, 18.6 s before the video does. Every second inside the cut that falls
# out of the 60 fps regime is a hitch second, 9 of them in 9 runs, none longer than 2 s, so
# nothing was removed from the middle. Menus, a dice game, dialogue and a sleep screen are inside
# the cut and in the regime.
#
# FIDELITY. The capture ran the policy the tree ships, so the two lines are comparable. The
# replay reads synth 0.5% against 0.5% (0.5% on the dejitter arm, which is how the stream ran),
# worst run 20 against 20 at the same present, runs >= 50 0 against 0 and pull wraps 29 against
# 29. Counted over this window, blends are 599 against 606, repeats 412 against 410, skips 78
# against 79, and lock releases 1 against 1 at the same present. The replay makes 67 moves, 65
# planned and 2 late, and refuses 21; the field's log has 68 moves in the window. The 7 blends,
# 2 repeats, 1 skip and 1 move by which the two differ were not traced present by present.
#
# Bounds on the REPLAY (not the field): inequalities, so an improvement passes and only a
# regression fails. Measured on the policy the capture ran.
max_worst_run 20
max_long_runs 0
max_synth_pct 0.9
min_reseeds 23
max_pull_wraps 29
extra_lag_ms 75
arrivals 222204
